\title{scmarkeragent: Evidence-Grounded Cell-Type Annotation for Seurat Objects}
\description{
Annotates single-cell RNA-seq clusters by measuring curated marker panels in the data and letting a language model decide which identity those measurements support, with every claim resolving to a publication and its source sentence. Reads Seurat .rds objects natively and runs from raw counts, against one shared configuration, one set of prompts and one marker resource.
}
\details{
The package is a thin, validated entry point over the two-arm scMarkerAgent
pipeline. The pipeline itself -- the same `rflow/` sources the benchmarks ran,
with the shared configuration, prompts, schemas and viewer assets -- ships
under `inst/scmarkeragent/` and runs in its own `Rscript` process, so this
package's namespace stays small: [annotate()] to run, [check_input()] to
route formats, and [download_resources()] / [verify_resources()] /
[resource_index()] to manage the curated marker resource.
